messages.content:
{
  "message": "I’m sorry you’re seeing “No Service.” I can help. My plan is to check two things in parallel: (1) your account/line status on our side (suspension, provisioning), and (2) quick on-device checks (airplane mode, SIM, settings) that commonly cause “No Service.” Once we have these, we’ll know whether to fix an account issue or guide a device-side fix.",
  "requested_info": {
    "identification": "Please provide ONE of the following so I can look up your line: (a) the phone number of the affected line, or (b) your customer ID, or (c) your full name AND date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
    "context_questions": [
      "What phone are you using (iPhone or Android, and model if you know)?",
      "Your current location (city/state) and if you recently traveled out of your usual area or abroad?",
      "Did this start suddenly today, and did anything change recently (SIM/eSIM swap, plan change, new phone, software update)?",
      "Do others around you on the same carrier have service right now?"
    ]
  },
  "quick_checks_for_you": [
    "Look at the status bar at the top of your phone and tell me exactly what you see: Is there an airplane icon? Do you see any signal bars or does it say “No Service” or “SOS”? Do you see a network type like 5G/4G/LTE?",
    "If you see an airplane icon, please turn Airplane Mode OFF. If it’s already OFF, please toggle it ON for 5 seconds and then OFF again to refresh the radios.",
    "Check for SIM messages: do you see “No SIM,” “SIM not provisioned,” or “SIM locked/PUK”? If you see SIM locked, don’t guess the PIN—tell me what it says.",
    "If it still shows No Service after the toggle, please reboot the phone (power it off, wait 20 seconds, power it back on) and let me know if anything changes."
  ],
  "notes": "Once you share your identification details, I’ll immediately check your line for suspension or provisioning issues. In the meantime, the quick checks above often resolve transient radio/SIM states. Please share the results of each step and the identification info so I can proceed on both fronts."
}

