{
  "message": "Thanks for trying. Since data was restored but MMS still won’t send, the most likely causes are a stale data session, APN/MMSC settings, Wi‑Fi Calling interference, or app permissions. Let’s refresh the connection first, then check settings. I’ll explain each step and why, and we’ll test after each change.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Refresh your radio/data session",
      "why": "After adding data, the phone sometimes keeps an old data session that blocks MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Turn Airplane Mode ON for ~10 seconds, then OFF.",
        "Alternatively, turn Mobile Data OFF, wait 5 seconds, then ON.",
        "Wait for signal and 4G/LTE/5G to return, then try sending an MMS (a small photo is best)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reboot your phone",
      "why": "A full restart cleanly re-registers on the network and refreshes MMS services.",
      "how": [
        "Restart the device.",
        "After it’s back up and you see 4G/LTE/5G, try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reset APN to defaults (then reboot)",
      "why": "MMS depends on the MMSC in your APN. If it’s missing or incorrect, MMS fails even when data works.",
      "how": [
        "Android path (may vary slightly): Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the 3‑dot menu > Reset to default.",
        "Restart the phone after resetting APN.",
        "When it reconnects to 4G/LTE/5G, try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Temporarily turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF",
      "why": "Some configurations can interfere with MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling > turn OFF.",
        "Try sending an MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm Messaging app permissions",
      "why": "MMS needs SMS and Storage access to send media.",
      "how": [
        "Long‑press your Messages app icon > App info > Permissions.",
        "Ensure SMS (or Phone/SMS) and Photos/Media/Storage are Allowed.",
        "Try sending an MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional quick checks",
      "why": "These can also block MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Ensure Network Mode is set to 4G/5G preferred: Settings > Mobile network > Preferred network type.",
        "Make sure Data Saver is OFF: Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver.",
        "If you use a VPN, disconnect it and try again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
