  "message": "I can help. When a phone shows “No Service,” the two most common causes are either an account/line issue (e.g., suspension) or a device/network setting issue (e.g., Airplane Mode, SIM, network mode, APN). Here’s my plan: 1) Verify your account and line status to rule out any suspension or provisioning issues. 2) Run a few quick checks on your phone to restore signal if it’s a device-side issue.",
  "questions": [
    "What’s the phone number of the affected line? (I’ll use this to verify your account and line status.)",
    "If you don’t have the number handy, please provide your full name and date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD) for verification.",
    "What city/state are you currently in? Is anyone around you on the same carrier also having issues?",
    "What phone do you have (iPhone or Android, model if known)?",
    "Has this line ever worked at your current location, or is this the first time you’re using it here?"
  ],
  "device_checks": {
    "instructions": [
      "On your phone, please run check_status_bar and share exactly what it shows (Airplane Mode, signal strength, network type like 5G/4G, Data Enabled/Disabled, Wi‑Fi/VPN icons, battery).",
      "Run check_sim_status and share the result (Active, Missing, or Locked).",
      "If you know how, also run check_network_status and share the results (signal strength, network type, mobile data enabled, data roaming status)."
    ],
    "quick_fixes_to_try_now": [
      "Toggle Airplane Mode: turn it ON for 10 seconds, then OFF.",
      "If it still says No Service, restart the phone (power off and back on).",
      "If check_sim_status shows Missing, power off, remove and reinsert the SIM carefully, then power on."
    ],
    "note": "Please tell me the results of each step. I’ll use your line info to check for any suspension or provisioning issues in parallel once you share your phone number."
  }
}

