  "message": "Good progress—your service and data are healthy, so this now looks like an MMS configuration issue. The most common remaining cause is the APN/MMSC settings, followed by app/data restrictions.",
  "thought_process": "MMS requires a valid MMSC URL in your APN, plus the messaging app must be allowed to use data and storage. Since Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF and data is Excellent, we’ll verify APN/MMSC first, then check for data restrictions and app permissions.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Check APN/MMSC settings (top fix for MMS)",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_apn_settings and tell me: the APN name and whether an MMSC URL is shown.",
        "If the MMSC field is missing/blank or looks incorrect: run reset_apn_settings, then run reboot_device.",
        "After the reboot, keep Wi‑Fi OFF and try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm network mode (should already be fine)",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_network_mode_preference. If it shows 2G or 3G, set set_network_mode_preference to \"4g_5g_preferred\", then retry MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rule out data restrictions",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF, then try MMS again.",
        "Run check_vpn_status. If a VPN is connected, run disconnect_vpn, then try MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify messaging app permissions",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_app_permissions with app_name=\"messaging\".",
        "If \"storage\" or \"sms\" aren’t granted, run grant_app_permission for each missing one (permission=\"storage\" and permission=\"sms\").",
        "Try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional quick MMS diagnostic",
      "actions": [
        "Run can_send_mms and share the result—it may point directly to APN/MMSC or permissions."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What does check_apn_settings show (APN name and MMSC URL)?",
    "If you reset APN settings and rebooted, did MMS start working?",
    "What are the results of check_data_restriction_status, check_vpn_status, and check_app_permissions for the messaging app?"
  ],
  "tip": "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF during these tests so we validate MMS over mobile data."
}

messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for trying. If the Wi‑Fi switch won’t stay ON, we’ll refresh the radios and verify status step‑by‑step. I’ll explain why each step helps and what to share back.",
  "thought_process": "A Wi‑Fi radio that stays OFF is usually caused by radios stuck after prior network changes, Airplane Mode conflicts, or a software toggle that didn’t apply. Cycling Airplane Mode resets all radios, then we try enabling Wi‑Fi from the system. If something else (like a VPN) is interfering, we’ll disable it. A reboot at the end refreshes the Wi‑Fi driver.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Check current indicators",
      "why": "Confirm Airplane Mode and current Wi‑Fi state.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_status_bar and share what you see for Wi‑Fi and Airplane Mode.",
        "Run check_wifi_status and share the output."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cycle Airplane Mode",
      "why": "This resets all wireless radios (cellular, Wi‑Fi, Bluetooth) and often frees a stuck Wi‑Fi toggle.",
      "actions": [
        "Run toggle_airplane_mode to turn Airplane Mode ON. Wait 10 seconds.",
        "Run toggle_airplane_mode again to turn Airplane Mode OFF."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn Wi‑Fi ON via system toggle",
      "why": "Attempt to enable the Wi‑Fi radio after the reset.",
      "actions": [
        "Run toggle_wifi to turn Wi‑Fi ON.",
        "Run check_wifi_status and share the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rule out VPN interference",
      "why": "Some VPN profiles can block or delay Wi‑Fi initialization.",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_vpn_status and share the result.",
        "If a VPN is connected, run disconnect_vpn, then run toggle_wifi again and check_wifi_status."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Full refresh",
      "why": "A reboot reloads the Wi‑Fi driver if it’s stuck.",
      "actions": [
        "Run reboot_device.",
        "After the phone restarts, run check_wifi_status and share the result."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_share": [
    "The outputs of check_status_bar and check_wifi_status from step 1.",
    "Whether Airplane Mode cycled successfully in step 2.",
    "The check_wifi_status result after step 3 (and after step 4 if a VPN was disconnected).",
    "The check_wifi_status result after the reboot in step 5."
  ],
  "note": "If Wi‑Fi still won’t turn ON after these steps, it may indicate a device-specific software or hardware issue. We’ll review your results and, if needed, I can transfer you to a human agent for advanced troubleshooting or recommend contacting your device’s support."
}

