messages.content:
{
  "message": "Wi‑Fi is ON but not joining your SSID. That usually points to saved credentials, a password/handshake mismatch, or a router-side issue. Let’s methodically rejoin your network and rule out the router.",
  "thought_process": "We’ll first clear any stale credentials by forgetting the network, then re-enter the password carefully. If that still fails, we’ll try a different band/SSID, then restart the router, and finally isolate whether it’s the phone or the Wi‑Fi by testing another network.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Forget the network and rejoin",
      "why": "Clears any bad saved credentials/handshake.",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Wi‑Fi > tap the “i” next to your home SSID > Forget This Network > Forget.",
        "Stay on the Wi‑Fi screen, wait for your SSID to reappear, tap it.",
        "Enter the Wi‑Fi password exactly (use “Show Password” if available), then Join."
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Wi‑Fi.",
        "Tap your home SSID (or Saved networks) > Forget.",
        "Return to the available networks list, tap your SSID, and re-enter the password."
      ],
      "after": [
        "Run check_wifi_status and tell me if it shows Connected to [SSID], or any error like Incorrect password/Authentication error/Saved."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Try the other band or guest network (if available)",
      "why": "Some phones prefer 2.4 GHz vs 5 GHz, or the router may have separate SSIDs.",
      "actions": [
        "If your router shows separate names (like MyHome-2G and MyHome-5G), try the other one.",
        "If there’s a Guest network, try connecting to it as a test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Power-cycle the router",
      "why": "Refreshes Wi‑Fi radios/DHCP on the router in case it’s stuck.",
      "actions": [
        "Unplug the router’s power for 30 seconds.",
        "Plug it back in and wait 2 full minutes for Wi‑Fi to broadcast.",
        "On your phone, toggle Wi‑Fi OFF then ON (toggle_wifi), then select your SSID and enter the password again.",
        "Run check_wifi_status and share the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Isolate phone vs. router",
      "why": "Determines whether the issue is with your phone or the home network.",
      "actions": [
        "Try connecting your phone to a different known-good Wi‑Fi (work, cafe, or a personal hotspot from another phone).",
        "If it connects elsewhere, your phone’s Wi‑Fi is fine and the home router likely needs attention.",
        "If it fails everywhere, we’ll look deeper at the phone."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "After forgetting and rejoining, what exact message do you see (Incorrect password, Authentication error, Saved, Connected without internet, or still not connected)?",
    "Do other devices at home connect to this Wi‑Fi successfully right now?",
    "Does your router broadcast separate 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz SSIDs, and if so, did you try both?",
    "What does check_wifi_status show after the router reboot and rejoin attempt?"
  ],
  "next_if_persists": "If it still won’t connect after trying the above and other devices are also failing, the router likely needs support from your internet/router provider. If other devices work but your phone doesn’t connect anywhere, tell me the exact error you see and we’ll proceed with additional device checks."
}

