{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. Since you’ve power-cycled the router, the next step is to try joining again and then isolate whether it’s a phone-side join issue or something about that SSID band.",
  "thought_process": "You’ve confirmed Wi‑Fi is ON and other devices connect, so the router is broadcasting. When one phone won’t join, it’s usually a credentials/handshake issue, band compatibility, or a device-side setting like MAC randomization. We’ll try a clean rejoin, then test alternate networks to isolate.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Join your SSID again after the router reboot",
      "why": "The router needed time to fully broadcast after reboot.",
      "actions": [
        "Wait a full 2 minutes after the router came back up.",
        "On your phone, toggle Wi‑Fi OFF and then ON.",
        "Select your home SSID and enter the password carefully (enable “Show password” while typing if available).",
        "After attempting to join, run check_wifi_status and share what it shows (Connected to [SSID], Incorrect password, Authentication error, Saved, or still not connected)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Try a different network on the same router",
      "why": "Quick isolation of band/SSID-specific issues.",
      "actions": [
        "If your router has a Guest network, try connecting to it.",
        "If you tried the 5 GHz SSID just now, also try the 2.4 GHz SSID (or vice versa) once more after the reboot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Test a different known-good Wi‑Fi",
      "why": "Isolates phone vs. home router.",
      "actions": [
        "Try connecting to another Wi‑Fi (work/cafe) or a personal hotspot from another phone.",
        "If it connects elsewhere, your phone’s Wi‑Fi is working and we should look at router-side settings for that SSID.",
        "If it fails everywhere, it points to a device-side setting we can adjust."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Advanced device checks (choose based on your phone type)",
      "why": "MAC randomization or network stacks can block joining.",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Wi‑Fi > tap the “i” next to your SSID > turn OFF “Private Wi‑Fi Address” (as a test) and try joining again.",
        "If still failing: Settings > General > Transfer or Reset > Reset > Reset Network Settings (this forgets Wi‑Fi/Bluetooth). Then try joining your SSID again."
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Wi‑Fi > (your SSID) > Forget. Then in Wi‑Fi’s advanced/Privacy settings, set MAC address type to Phone/Device MAC (not Randomized) as a test. Rejoin your SSID.",
