{
  "message": "Understood. Your line has data available and roaming is enabled on our side. Since you now have signal and mobile data with Data Roaming ON, the likely blockers are on-device: APN/MMSC configuration not fully applied, network mode, or app defaults/permissions. We will verify mobile data works off Wi‑Fi, run the MMS diagnostic, then reset APN to default and retest.",
  "thought_process": [
    "MMS requires working mobile data plus correct MMS server (MMSC) and proper app permissions.",
    "You already turned off Wi‑Fi Calling, VPN, and Data Saver. We will not repeat those.",
    "Even if MMSC looks populated, an APN reset often resolves hidden field mismatches. A reboot is required after the reset."
  ],
  "steps_now_android": [
    {
      "step": "Verify mobile data independently",
      "actions": [
        "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF.",
        "Open your browser and go to example.com.",
        "Report whether the page loads over mobile data."
      ],
      "reason": "Confirms mobile data is actually working, which MMS depends on."
    },
    {
      "step": "Run MMS diagnostic",
      "actions": [
        "Use can_send_mms on your phone and share the result."
      ],
      "reason": "Shows if the messaging app can reach the MMS service."
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm preferred network mode",
      "actions": [
        "Use check_network_mode_preference and share the result.",
        "If it shows 2G/3G, change to 4g_5g_preferred."
      ],
      "reason": "Older modes can block or slow MMS; 4G/5G is required."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reset APN to default (even if MMSC appears correct)",
      "actions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > Access Point Names.",
        "Menu (⋮) > Reset to default."
      ],
      "reason": "Restores all MMS-related fields (including hidden ones) to carrier defaults."
    },
    {
      "step": "Reboot to apply APN",
      "actions": [
        "Restart the phone.",
        "Wait 60–90 seconds for network registration.",
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF, ensure Mobile Data ON and Data Roaming ON."
      ],
      "reason": "Ensures the phone reloads the new APN settings."
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm Messages app defaults and permissions",
      "actions": [
        "Settings > Apps > See all apps > Messages.",
        "Permissions: allow SMS (or Text) and Files and media/Storage.",
        "Settings > Apps > Default apps > SMS app > select Messages."
      ],
      "reason": "Missing SMS/Storage permissions or a different default app can block MMS."
    },
    {
      "step": "Retest MMS",
      "actions": [
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF, send a small photo MMS to your own number or a contact."
      ],
      "reason": "Validates that MMS now works with corrected settings."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "Does example.com load over mobile data with Wi‑Fi OFF?",
    "Result of can_send_mms.",
    "Result of check_network_mode_preference (and whether you set it to 4g_5g_preferred).",
    "After APN reset + reboot: did the MMS send? If it failed, provide the exact behavior/error (e.g., spinning, “Not sent,” or a specific message).",
    "If possible, also share the current status bar readout (signal bars and network type) using check_status_bar, and the summary from check_network_status."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Your account/line is Active, roaming is enabled, and you have refueled data this cycle.",
    "We will proceed to additional checks only if MMS still fails after these steps."
  ]
}

