  "message": "Your phone is reporting that it can’t see a SIM, which prevents any cellular service and MMS. Let’s fix that by reseating the SIM (if you use a physical SIM) or checking your eSIM line status. We already added 2 GB of data, so once the SIM is recognized and you have signal, MMS should work.",
  "why_this_works": [
    "A missing/not-seated SIM blocks network registration entirely.",
    "Reseating often resolves contact/placement issues; if you use eSIM, ensuring the eSIM line is ON restores service."
  ],
  "first_confirm": "Are you using a physical SIM card (there’s a SIM tray) or an eSIM (no physical SIM)? If you’re not sure, look for a SIM tray hole on the phone’s edge. If there’s no tray, you likely use eSIM.",
  "steps_physical_sim": [
    {
      "step": "Power off and remove SIM",
      "instructions": [
        "Power the phone OFF.",
        "Use a SIM eject tool/paperclip to open the SIM tray.",
        "Remove the SIM, inspect the gold contacts (no scratches/bends), and gently wipe with a soft, dry cloth.",
        "Check the tray/slot for dust and the SIM orientation (match the notch)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Reinsert and restart",
      "instructions": [
        "Reinsert the SIM flat in the tray; push the tray back in fully and flush.",
        "Power ON the phone and wait up to 60 seconds."
      ],
      "what_to_check": "Do you now see signal bars (3G/4G/LTE/5G)? Does SIM status change from ‘No SIM’ to ‘Active/Ready’?"
    }
  ],
  "steps_esim": [
    {
      "step": "Ensure eSIM line is ON",
      "instructions": [
        "Go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > SIMs/Mobile Network.",
        "Locate your carrier line and ensure the toggle is ON.",
        "If it shows ‘No SIM’ or no eSIM profile is listed, let me know."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Restart",
      "instructions": [
        "Restart the phone to force a fresh network registration.",
        "After boot, wait up to 60 seconds for bars to appear."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "isolation_if_still_missing": [
    "If possible, test your SIM in another phone OR insert a known‑good SIM into this phone:",
    "- If your SIM works in another phone, the issue is likely this phone’s SIM slot/eSIM configuration.",
    "- If your SIM is still not detected elsewhere (or a known‑good SIM isn’t detected in this phone), the SIM may be faulty and needs replacement."
  ],
  "next_after_signal_returns": [
    "With Wi‑Fi OFF, load a website to confirm mobile data works.",
    "Send an MMS (photo) to yourself or a contact."
  ],
  "what_to_reply_with": [
    "1) Are you on physical SIM or eSIM?",
    "2) After following the relevant steps, does the phone now detect the SIM and show signal bars?",
    "3) If not, were you able to test with another phone/SIM, and what happened?",
    "4) If you now have signal, could you load a webpage and send an MMS successfully?"
  ],
  "if_unresolved": "If the SIM still isn’t detected after reseating/checking eSIM and the simple swap test, I can transfer you to a human agent to arrange a SIM replacement or assist with eSIM reprovisioning."
}

