    "2G is generally not suitable for MMS. Switching your Preferred network type to 4G/5G (or LTE) will allow MMS to send once signal attaches."
  ],
  "steps_on_your_phone": [
    {
      "step": "Set Preferred network to 4G/5G",
      "instructions": [
        "Go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network/Cellular.",
        "Tap Preferred network type.",
        "Select 4G/5G preferred (or LTE/5G). If you also have an option for 4G/LTE only, choose that temporarily to avoid falling back to 2G."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Let the phone reattach",
      "instructions": [
        "Wait 10–20 seconds and watch the status bar.",
        "You should see 4G/LTE/5G (or at least 3G) with some signal bars.",
        "If it still shows 2G or no bars: toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then OFF. If still stuck, reboot the phone once."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Improve signal if needed",
      "instructions": [
        "If signal remains poor, move near a window or go outdoors briefly and watch if it upgrades to 3G/4G/5G."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Test mobile data",
      "instructions": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF. Open a browser and load example.com or any site."
      ]
    },
