messages.content:
{
  "message": "Given you now have excellent 5G and fast mobile data, the most likely blockers are on-device: messaging app permissions/restrictions, APN/MMSC not fully applied, or a VPN/app conflict. I’ll walk you through targeted checks and fixes, and explain why each matters.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "MMS depends on mobile data plus a valid MMSC in APN.",
    "If Data Saver or app background data is restricted, MMS can silently fail.",
    "If the messaging app lacks Storage/Photos or SMS permissions, it can’t attach/send media.",
    "A VPN can interfere with MMS routing on some devices."
  ],
  "steps_on_your_phone": [
    {
      "step": "Turn OFF Data Saver / remove global data restrictions",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Data Saver.",
        "If Data Saver is ON, turn it OFF."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Ensure the messaging app has required permissions",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Apps > your default Messaging app > Permissions.",
        "Allow: Storage/Photos (or Files and media) and SMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Allow background/unrestricted data for the messaging app",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Apps > your default Messaging app > Mobile data (or Data usage).",
        "Turn ON Background data.",
        "If available, turn ON Unrestricted data usage (to bypass Data Saver)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Disable any active VPN",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > VPN.",
        "If a VPN shows as Connected, Disconnect it and try again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify APN shows an MMSC URL",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Open the active APN and confirm there is an MMSC field populated.",
        "If MMSC is missing, use Reset to default again and then reboot once more."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Test MMS again",
      "instructions": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF.",
        "Open your messaging app and send a photo to yourself or a contact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "If still failing, run two quick diagnostics",
      "instructions": [
        "1) can_send_mms diagnostic in your phone’s troubleshooting menu and share the result.",
        "2) If available, check_app_permissions/app status for Messaging to confirm the above settings took effect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Optional isolation test",
      "instructions": [
        "If you’re using a third‑party messaging app, try sending the MMS using the phone’s default Messages app to rule out an app‑specific issue."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_reply_with": [
    "1) Is Data Saver OFF now?",
    "2) Do the Messaging app permissions show Storage/Photos and SMS as Allowed?",
    "3) Are Background data and (if present) Unrestricted data usage enabled for the Messaging app?",
    "4) Is a VPN connected? If so, did disconnecting it help?",
    "5) In APN settings, is the MMSC field present after the reset/reboot?",
    "6) After these changes, what happens when you try to send an MMS? If you can run the can_send_mms check, what does it report?"
  ],
  "next_steps_if_still_failing_after_all_above": [
    "I’ll escalate to a human agent to review backend MMS provisioning and logs on your line. I’ll include everything we’ve already tried so you don’t repeat steps."
  ],
  "note": "Your data cap is no longer a blocker—we added 2 GB. Once the device-side settings are correct, MMS should send normally."
}

